  "headline": "Palantir\u2019s recent financial growth is strong, but its high valuation and large share-price swings do not support calling it \u201cthe safest stock on earth.\u201d",
  "claim_checks": [
   {
    "claim_id": "C1",
    "verdict": "contradicted",
    "explanation": "The company has had strong recent results\u2014revenue grew 56.2% and net income grew 251.6% in the latest annual figures (E1)\u2014but its shares had 60.8% annualized volatility and a 48.2% maximum drawdown over the measured year (E4). Over five years, the maximum drawdown was 77.6% and annualized volatility was 67.0% (E3), which is inconsistent with an absolute safety claim.",
