     "E1",
     "E3",
     "E4"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "red_flags": [
   "The absolute claim that this is \u201cthe safest stock on earth\u201d is not supported and ignores substantial share-price risk.",
   "The share price had a 48.2% maximum drawdown over the measured year and 77.6% over five years (E4, E3).",
   "The trailing P/E was 174.12 and price-to-sales ratio was 76.8, so the valuation is demanding (E2)."
  ],
  "what_the_tip_left_out": [
   "Revenue, net income, and operating cash flow all increased in the latest annual figures, by 56.2%, 251.6%, and 85.0%, respectively (E1).",
   "Despite those results, the stock\u2019s one-year return of 12.1% lagged the S&P 500\u2019s 15.0% return over the same period (E4).",
   "The valuation was high: trailing P/E was 174.12 and price-to-sales was 76.8 (E2)."
  ],
  "questions_before_buying": [
   "Could you tolerate a loss like the 48.2% maximum drawdown recorded over the measured year (E4)?",
   "What assumptions about future growth would need to hold to justify a trailing P/E of 174.12 and price-to-sales ratio of 76.8 (E2)?",
   "Is this claim based on current financial filings and a clearly defined measure of safety, or just the source\u2019s opinion?"
  ],
  "risk_level": "high",
  "plain_english_summary": "Palantir\u2019s latest annual figures show strong revenue growth, profit, and operating cash generation (E1). That is a positive business picture, but it does not make the stock safe: its price has swung sharply and its valuation is high (E2, E3, E4). \u201cSafest stock on earth\u201d is an absolute claim the evidence does not establish. Past returns and company results cannot guarantee how the share price will behave next."
 },
